This approach should work better because:
- We're no longer trying to import any Node.js modules
- The preview will render consistently in the browser
- We maintain the same props interface (params and searchParams)
- We provide a realistic preview of how the actual component would look

The mock component includes common elements you might find in an app page:
- App title and description
- Markdown content rendering
- App details like categories and price
- Basic styling classes that match common patterns

This should resolve the `fs` module error while still providing a meaningful preview of the component.

